---
id: org.dxos.scene
name: Scene
version: 0.1.0
---

One data structure for 2D drawings and 3D scenes. The editor, the assistant and the animator all read and write it.
`@dxos/scene` holds the schemas, validation, layout and the ECHO form; `@dxos/diagram` holds its text form (the
`scene`, `camera` and `element` statements of `.dx`); `@dxos/react-ui-scene` draws it; plugin-canvas makes it an
animator stage. The design is `agents/superpowers/specs/2026-10-28-scene-model-design.md`.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term       | URI                         |
| ---------- | --------------------------- |
| `type`     | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`     |
| `feat`     | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`     |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |

## Types

```mdl
type Scene
  desc: >
    The shape both dimensions share, over an element type E and a camera type C: `Scene<E, C>`. Its elements are
    records inside the one scene object.
  fields:
    name?: string
    theme?: string
    component?: boolean             # a reusable scene that instance elements place
    camera: C
    elements: Record<string, E>
```

```mdl
type Scene2D
  desc: >
    `Scene<Element2D, Camera2D>` as an ECHO object. ECHO reserves `id`, so the scene's own id is `key`.
  typename: org.dxos.type.scene.scene2d
  fields:
    key: string
```

```mdl
type Scene3D
  desc: `Scene<Element3D, Camera3D>` as an ECHO object, keyed as Scene2D is.
  typename: org.dxos.type.scene.scene3d
  fields:
    key: string
```

```mdl
type BaseElement
  desc: >
    Every item in a scene: a shape, a link, a label, a group, a child scene or an instance. Its `kind` says which.
    The fields below are shared; geometry comes from the scene type.
  fields:
    id: string                      # fixed when the element is created
    kind: string
    order?: string                  # paint order; z is depth
    layer?: string
    hidden?: boolean
    locked?: boolean
    label?: string
    style?: Style
    from?: Binding                  # a link's ends
    to?: Binding
    members?: string[]              # a group's elements
    layout?: Layout                 # an arrangement a group applies to its members
    pinned?: boolean                # placed by a person; layout leaves it
    child?: Ref<Scene2D | Scene3D>  # a child scene's element
    props?: Record<string, any>     # kind-specific fields
```

```mdl
type Element2D
  desc: BaseElement with 2D geometry, in canvas pixels.
  fields:
    center?: Vec2
    size?: Size2
    rotation?: number
```

```mdl
type Element3D
  desc: BaseElement with 3D geometry, in scene units; `scale` is the element's size.
  fields:
    center?: Vec3
    scale?: Vec3
    rotation?: Vec3                 # Euler degrees
```

```mdl
type Style
  desc: Semantic style tokens shared by both dimensions; a theme resolves them to CSS in 2D and materials in 3D.
  fields:
    hue?: string
    tone?: number
    surface?: string                # solid | tint | glass | none
    border?: boolean
    rounded?: boolean
    opacity?: number
```

```mdl
type Camera3D
  desc: Where a 3D view looks from; angles in degrees, yaw 0 from the front, pitch above the horizon.
  fields:
    target: Vec3
    yaw: number
    pitch: number
    distance: number
    fov: number
    projection: string              # perspective | orthographic
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: One model for 2D and 3D

  req F-1.1: A scene is one ECHO object, Scene2D or Scene3D, whose elements are records inside it; types are shared only where 2D and 3D share properties.
  req F-1.2: There is one record kind, Element, for shapes and links alike; a link's ends are Bindings to other elements of its scene.
  req F-1.3: Element ids are never positional, and the id `camera` is reserved for the animator's camera target.
  req F-1.4: A child scene is an element holding a Ref to another Scene object; it keeps its own units and is scaled to fit its frame.
  req F-1.5: A group keeps its members in its parent's coordinates, and stores its arrangement so layout can be re-run; a pinned member is not moved.
  req F-1.6: A solid is an operation tree (union, difference, extrude) over operand elements, recomputed when drawn.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: The text form

  req F-2.1: Records print to `.dx` text and parse back to the same records; printing a parsed canonical document returns the same text.
  req F-2.2: Text that gives a group's arrangement but not its members' positions is laid out when parsed.
  req F-2.3: Parsing reports duplicate ids, the reserved id, kinds from the other dimension, unbound links, missing members and missing child scenes.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Drawing and animation

  req F-3.1: 2D scenes draw through react-ui-canvas, 3D scenes through Babylon, and a 2D scene may also be drawn in 3D on the ground plane.
  req F-3.2: A renderer skips a link whose end is missing and stops at a child scene already on its path.
  req F-3.3: Each scene type is an animator stage whose targets are its root scene's drawn elements, keyed by their annotated paths.
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Share a type between 2D and 3D only where they share properties; embedding one dimension in the other is a separate mechanism, not a reason to share a root type.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Do not distinguish nodes from links: every item in a scene is one kind of record, as in tldraw.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element, F-1.2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The record is called Element, the container Scene, and reusable parts Component and Instance.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element, Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A scene is stored as records inside one ECHO object.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D, F-1.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: The records are the source of truth; the DSL is a lossless text form of them.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A solid is stored as an operation tree over operand elements and recomputed when loaded, not as a baked mesh.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.6]
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Both groups and child scenes exist: a group keeps its members in its parent's coordinates, a child scene has its own and is a separate object.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.4, F-1.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A 2D scene can be rendered through a 3D projection.
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.1]
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A link's ends are Bindings (element id and optional anchor); moving an element moves what is bound to it. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.2]
  why: With one record kind, a link's geometry must come from what it connects, as tldraw's bindings do.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Paint order is `order` and `z` is depth; element ids are fixed at creation and never positional. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element, F-1.3]
  why: Animator tracks and DSL edits refer to element ids, and a 3D z cannot share a name with paint order.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Layout intent is stored on groups as an arrangement, alongside the positions it produces; a hand-placed element is pinned. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.5, F-2.2]
  why: Storing positions keeps renderers and the animator free of layout; storing intent lets layout be re-run.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Each scene and each component is its own ECHO object, and a child scene is reached by Ref. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.4]
  why: Undo, sharing and an animator shot each bind to one scene.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: A child scene keeps its own units, scaled to 80% of its frame; a link binds only within its own scene. Fills in [D-7].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.4]
  why: The same rule canvas portals use, so a nested scene reads the same in 2D and 3D.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: Style tokens are shared and a theme resolves them per renderer; glass in the presentation theme is a rim shell. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Style, F-3.1]
  why: The tokens have the same meaning in both dimensions; only how they look differs.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: A lifted 2D scene maps canvas (x, y) to (x/100, 0, −y/100), so its top-down view matches the canvas. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-28
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-3.1]
  why: Canvas y runs down the screen, which is −z seen from above at yaw 0.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: The plugin still owns a canvas object, which carries its additional metadata, but the editing, rendering and animation mechanism depends only on `Scene`.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-17: One canvas object type serves both dimensions: its root Ref points at a `Scene2D` or a `Scene3D`, and the editor picks the viewport from the root.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-18: 3D move, rotate and scale handles are Babylon's `GizmoManager` gizmos.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-19: The 3D viewer orbits, zooms and pans with the mouse; inside an animator stage the animation drives the camera.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-20: Every drawing is a `Drawing`, so one query finds them all and a user can convert one format into another. `Drawing.content` is a Ref to one content type, each owned by its plugin: `Excalidraw`, `TLDraw` or `Canvas`. plugin-canvas's `Canvas` holds its metadata, including named style classes, and `Canvas.content` is a Ref to a `Scene2D` or `Scene3D`.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
  supersedes: D-17
```

```mdl
decision D-21: plugin-spacetime is deleted within stage 3, once each of its tools has a test in the new editor; its objects are not migrated.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
```

```mdl
decision D-22: plugin-canvas switches to `Scene2D` only when every react-ui-canvas mode runs on it: free, lattice, constrained and scored.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D]
```

```mdl
decision D-23: The fields every element shares are the type `BaseElement`; `Element2D` and `Element3D` add their geometry to it.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [BaseElement, Element2D, Element3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-24: A 3D element's location is `center`, as a 2D element's is, not `position`.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Element3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-25: Both dimensions share one generic `Scene<E, C>` type, over the element and camera types; `Scene2D` and `Scene3D` are built from it.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene, Scene2D, Scene3D]
```

```mdl
decision D-26: `Drawing.canvas` is widened rather than replaced: its Ref accepts the existing `Drawing.Canvas`, which tldraw and excalidraw drawings keep unchanged and unmigrated, or plugin-canvas's typed `Canvas`. Only `dxos.org/scene/2` drawings migrate, to a `Canvas` and a `Scene2D`. The `Canvas` and Scene parts of [D-20] stand.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Scene2D, Scene3D]
  supersedes: D-20
```
